{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-nagata-universally-Japanese}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b6864e001321fefbf2004fa24be3e69f77eb10b2263cf022fa6496045f656db", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBeing Nagata is the same thing as being locally Noetherian\nand universally Japanese, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b2780d0189779864e2f1675643600712ad1014881ba82b6f4cd6b461a8f60575", "unit_id": "tag:033R:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}/\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Spec(A) \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$A/\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0010": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\cite{Hoobler-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\cite[Example 1]{Hochster-loci}", "REF_0003": "\\cite{Heinzer-Levy}", "REF_0004": "\\cite[Expos\\'e XIX]{Traveaux}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-non-integral-Japanese}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f1fce65f0d698c398d205479c0b0f13f8bde13c1260d623a53718b1deadb8f72", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a495e0a4b4126f4b08d37a42a8db0c366a219766e7ceabdcfc2ced067b61451", "source_text": "In <REF_0001> a (locally Noetherian) scheme <MATH_0001> is called\nJapanese if for every <MATH_0002> and every associated prime <MATH_0003>\nof <MATH_0004> the ring <MATH_0005> is\nJapanese. We do not use this definition since there exists a one\ndimensional Noetherian domain with excellent (in particular\nJapanese) local rings whose normalization is not finite. See\n<REF_0002> or <REF_0003> or\n<REF_0004>.\nOn the other hand, we could circumvent this problem by calling a scheme\n<MATH_0006> Japanese if for every affine open <MATH_0007> the ring\n<MATH_0008> is Japanese for every associated prime <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c39f58df26c9f741553f6ad7ee5dda9842fe22c8606054ef2b16c935253ca4b", "unit_id": "tag:033T:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-nagata-locally-Noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50fdaa6f8663838073be303f14592c66628de208547b8a97557ae1c70f7c45ea", "source_text": "A Nagata scheme is locally Noetherian.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2c17e6a0ab773f5134399cb61ded747b5e2118df215f95f433fbc229f94f11e", "unit_id": "tag:033U:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:37ee2cf40b2e529386b1a876b08fa17b3bbb4daaa81a51839ac276e279f53810", "source_text": "This is true because a Nagata ring is Noetherian by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b79930bbe19c6beed72ceb768e067b40281edd4c1bb3d63b02e2adbfbf2d2505", "unit_id": "tag:033U:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "033R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-Japanese}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18e9a26b5fa458f2e63c7003c2a8c9ec4ca30f5ba1f3fb5d19f20d8da03f8373", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an integral scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the domain <MATH_0004>\nis Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005>\nsuch that each <MATH_0006> is Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is Japanese.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is Japanese then every open subscheme\nis Japanese.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a78823d9fc293ac8c1359795a1e44ae0d605c8ce23cbfb962fcff731e294c7ce", "unit_id": "tag:033V:statement"}
